---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Study Abroad Resource Centre | StudyPath"><main class="container py-12"><a class="text-sm font-bold text-teal-700" href={base}>← StudyPath home</a><div class="mt-7"><p class="eyebrow teal">LEARN & PREPARE</p><h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Study Abroad Resource Centre</h1><p class="muted mt-3 max-w-3xl">Practical preparation guides for students. This content is general educational guidance and should be checked against official institution and government requirements.</p></div>
<div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
<article id="applications" class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">University application basics</h2><ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm"><li>Choose a programme and read its official course page in full.</li><li>Check degree equivalency, subject prerequisites, grade thresholds and language tests.</li><li>Record the correct intake, application deadline, application fee and submission route.</li><li>Prepare transcripts, certificates, CV, motivation letter and references as requested.</li><li>Submit only through the official university portal and retain the confirmation.</li></ol><p class="muted mt-3 text-xs">Requirements differ by institution and applicant category.</p></article>
<article id="scholarships" class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Scholarship applications</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm"><li>Read the current call and confirm eligible nationalities, degree levels and fields.</li><li>Separate tuition waivers from stipends, travel grants, insurance and accommodation.</li><li>Check whether admission and scholarship applications use separate forms.</li><li>Prepare academic records, references, motivation statements and any required proposal.</li><li>Confirm whether the award is renewable and what academic conditions apply.</li></ul><p class="muted mt-3 text-xs">Never assume a funding reference means an award is currently open.</p></article>
<article id="english-tests" class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">IELTS, TOEFL and PTE</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm">Universities decide which English tests they accept and whether they require minimum scores in individual components. Check the exact programme page and the relevant admissions cycle. Do not assume that a Medium of Instruction letter replaces a test unless the institution explicitly confirms an exemption for your case. Keep score validity dates in mind when planning the application timeline.</p></article>
<article id="sop-cv" class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Statement of Purpose and academic CV</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm"><li>Explain your academic interests and why the specific programme fits them.</li><li>Connect prior coursework, projects, employment or research to your next study goal.</li><li>Use specific evidence instead of generic claims or copied templates.</li><li>Keep the CV accurate, chronological and easy to scan.</li><li>Follow each university's word limits and formatting instructions.</li></ul></article>
<article class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Recommendation letters</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm">Choose referees who know your academic or professional work well. Ask early, share the programme requirements and provide an accurate summary of your work. Confirm whether the university needs a confidential online reference or a signed letter.</p></article>
<article class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Research proposal</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm">For research degrees, check whether a proposal is required and whether a supervisor must be contacted first. A useful proposal normally explains the research question, background, method, feasibility and expected contribution. Follow the institution's own length and format guidance.</p></article>
<article class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Visa preparation</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm">Visa rules, financial evidence, work rights and processing times are determined by government authorities and can change. Use only the official immigration website or embassy/consulate instructions for your application location. StudyPath does not provide legal or immigration advice.</p></article>
<article class="surface p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Financial planning</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm">Budget for tuition, housing, food, transport, insurance, visa costs, travel and initial setup. Confirm what a scholarship actually covers and whether proof of funds is required separately. Use exchange rates and estimates that you enter yourself; costs vary by city and personal circumstances.</p></article>
</div></main></BaseLayout>